From 5e4d3ee96bfffcefb12f69f2fe12b6524dc305dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 03:00:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] deeptrace: print the brain's outputs on what it is shown, not
 on the raw senses

The brain readout in every trace was computed on the wrong inputs. `probe_full` fed the brain the
raw senses, but the tick hands it `brain_inputs()`, which under the Trail and TrailAway choosers
zeroes `PheroAAlong` and `PheroBAlong`. So every `o_`/`h` column `deeptrace` wrote, and the brain
readouts of `digbox`, `nestdoor` and `trailfollow`, printed outputs the tick never acted on
wherever those two inputs were nonzero.
- How often: on the goal box under the shipped walk those inputs are nonzero on 99% of empty
  decisions (seed 1, 50k-100k, 146,070 decisions).
- Before: under the needs walk (its own branch), 85% of 156,207 decisions whose step chance is the
  brain's own `Move` disagreed with the printed `o_Move`.
- After: on a shipped trace of seed 1, the printed `Move` equals the step chance the tick used on
  90% of empty, unpaced decisions. The rest carry other pace rules.
- The input columns were always right. Nothing in the simulation reads `probe_full`.

`Reports/instruments.md` now says, in deeptrace's entry, from when its `o_`/`h` columns can be
trusted.

Tested on main 927a3439: clippy `--all-targets --release --locked -D warnings` clean; `cargo test
--release --lib creature::`.

